From 3fee5b7e5255eff27a6d533ddff9ddbe3e61b025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 00:53:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/24] [WIP] oplus-fwk: port the OEM framework glue that OS16
 activates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Restoring the device's real OplusOS 16 version (the OplusBuild change)
makes the OEM apps take their OS16 code paths, which call framework classes
the LineageOS port had dropped. Without these the gallery main activity
dies on launch (com.oplus.util.OplusPlatformLevelUtils -> NoClassDefFoundError
in BaseActivity) and the camera-SDK APS metadata path can throw on
motion-photo capture (com.oplus.wrapper.hardware.camera2.* at SDK_VERSION>=34).

Port the handful an empirical OS16 sweep found to actually crash:
- com.oplus.util.OplusPlatformLevelUtils: the sole uncaught gallery crash;
  a simplified stub (getPlatformLevel -> LEVEL_HIGH; animation/gaussian from
  props) matching the 4 methods the gallery's PerformanceLevelUtils calls,
  without the OEM resource arrays.
- android.os.OplusKeyEventManager: add getInstance() + no-op register/
  unregister + LISTEN_* constants to the existing stub (avoids the
  OplusActivityTaskManager chain).
- com.oplus.wrapper.hardware.camera2.{CaptureResult,CameraCharacteristics,
  CameraMetadata,impl.CameraMetadataNative}: thin forwarders to the AOSP
  @hide camera2 metadata APIs (the getNativeMetadata()/getMetadataPtr()
  chain ApsUtils.getMetadataPtrForJni needs).

The other OS16-activated missing classes are all caught/degraded by the
gallery addon layer (no crash) and are intentionally left unported.

(cherry picked from commit 3b5a61a27cd18c156fb756cb6b6ab75bf4f51102)

Ledger: hardware_oplus.md Accepted Group C row 4 (3b5a61a2)
Stub-matrix: task-9-stub-inventory.md row M10 — consumer: OplusCamera loads the com.oplus.wrapper camera2 metadata wrappers once OS16 version is reported (stacks after 0f54be9d/K08); location: base wrapper/hardware/ contains only devicestate/; Task-10 container-rejected-all keeps it in the boot jar
